<title>LITHUANIA: BOURSE CAPITALISATION UP LAST WEEK.</title>
<headline>BOURSE CAPITALISATION UP LAST WEEK.</headline>
<dateline>VILNIUS 1997-07-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The capitalisation of the Vilnius</p>
<p>bourse rose to 5.329 billion litas last week from 5.186 billion</p>
<p>litas the previous week, the stock exchange said on Monday.</p>
<p>Vilnius bourse statistics:</p>
<p>					   June 30-July 04 June 23-27</p>
<p>    Submitted orders		  16,367	   16,985</p>
<p>    Executed orders		   1,106	    992</p>
<p>Number of transactions on</p>
<p>    Central market (CM)	     938		729</p>
<p>    Turnover on the CM in LTL     3,431,680	4,169,790</p>
<p>Number of transactions in</p>
<p>    block trades (BT)		 83		 130</p>
<p>    Turnover of BT in LTL	   9,321,960	16,440,800</p>
<p>    Supply of shares per week     59,467,564     60,766,923</p>
<p>    Demand of shares per week     5,094,725	3,605,856</p>
<p>Turnover of shares</p>
<p>    on CM per week in LTL	   1,991,520	1,925,950</p>
<p>    in BT per week in LTL	   9,321,960	6,360,130</p>
<p>The number of transactions</p>
<p>    in government T-bills	   18		 20</p>
<p>The turnover of government</p>
<p>    T-bills in LTL per week	 1,440,160	12,324,510</p>
<p>-- Andrius Vilkancas, Vilnius newsroom + 370 2 22 35 17</p>
